  "observations": {
    "layout": "One continuous four-sided enclosure with corner towers and offset grouped halls occupying the west/north interior. An open court band separates the south gateway from the halls; no extra building is counted per tower or hall.",
    "proportion": "The preserved whole is27x40x31; actual nonair spans y0..30. Upper y26..30 singleton roof/mast/banner states are recorded without deleting them or claiming occupied floors.",
    "facade": "Stone wall and repeated crenellation form a perimeter. Halls have internal facing windows and smaller adjoining volumes. Asymmetric tall corner and lower open corners support distinct high/low lookout hierarchy.",
    "roof": "Joined pitched hall volumes occupy the courtyard edge, plus one pointed high corner. This is structurally different from the open desert court and the low side hall in the two actual comparison images; changing material is not the reason.",
    "materials": "Actual palette replay confirms stone/stone-brick walls, timber roof and original ladder/door states. Classification colors and full-cell rendering cannot prove original texture, precise collision or surface quality.",
    "circulation": "Source lower doors and northeast ladder support gateway/court/hall/tower adjacency only. No native terrain or continuous route walk was performed.",
    "terrain": "The low continuous ground skirt belongs to the whole template. Original starts pool selects this body; external road/villager interfaces are neither reconstructed buildings nor independently credited references."
  },
